# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's WP2 evidence jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway
# commit of the integrated branch (tp4/fusion-1 with WP2 merged) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. ONE TAG AT A TIME; wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives the window (@SERVED_IMAGE@: the served image's
# reference; @K64J_GRAFT_DIR@ and @K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256@: the K64j graft directory and its binary's digest, the one-card harnesses). The harness is THIS CHECKOUT's scripts/ci run on card M alone
# (K64J_HARNESS=ordered_writer: ordered_writer_tp4_card_test.py with QWEN_FAST_TP=4 on one chip of four), so no new image is needed for the proof; C2_IMAGE_TAG is the programme's image.
# WHAT IT DECIDES (plan unknown U1): is bfloat8_b read-modify-write idempotent on the hardware packer? The served chain applies pack(unpack(.)) once PER ROW of a tile row, the page-parallel K/V
# writer (kv_page_writer_tp4, QWEN_FAST_KV_PAGE_WRITER) once PER TILE; they leave the same bytes exactly when pack(unpack(x)) is the identity on every block the packer writes. The page64 arm
# (ordered_writer_page_arm_tp4.py) writes the same pages through the served writer and the page writer on identical caches, K and V, both sources (prepared K/V interleaved in DRAM, and in the
# height-sharded L1 shards the AttnPrep op writes), the shapes the stack writes (four users of 16 consecutive positions: aligned, across the 32-row tile boundary, across the 64-token page
# boundary, the window's last positions), page-table widths 2,052 and 4,096, eager and trace replay, three payload regimes (bfloat8_b-exact from zero caches, which a host can predict; random
# non-exact bfloat16 over a random device-packed cache = partial pages; edge values: -0, denormals, an outlier that underflows its block mates, rounding carries, the largest and smallest
# normals), and compares the COMPLETE caches as bit patterns after every step; it then writes the same page twice, and writes every stored row of a device-packed cache back to where it came
# from with the served writer and with the page writer (the cache must not change by one bit).
# The lever refuses to engage (it logs one '[PINDIAG] tp4 kv page writer fell back' line and the chained writer runs) unless ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json carries a 'page_writer' block bound to
# the live design: that block exists only after a PASS of the full job below is recorded.
# W2 (the proof): the page64 arm at full scope - every regime, both sources, all three modes, both widths, seeds 0, 1 and 2, K and V - plus the write-back cases of the served and the page
# writer. (ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json already holds the E1 record for the chained and the 32-row writers, so this run is page-only.)
# PASS: 'ORDERED_WRITER verdict=... page=PASS page_scope=full page_checks=N page_exact=N'. Then, from the report this run uploads:
#   py -3.11 -B scripts/ci/record_ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.py --merge-page --report <report> --run <run id> --tag <experiment tag> --commit <40-hex> --image <tag name>
# which adds the 'page_writer' block to ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json (bound to kv_page_writer_tp4.design_signature(), checked against the LIVE kernel before anything is written) and re-pins
# ORDERED_WRITER_EVIDENCE_TP4_SHA256 in page_width_tp4.py; commit both by explicit path. Any later edit of kv_page_writer_tp4.cpp or of the geometry changes the signature and the lever refuses again.
# A FAIL here is the answer to U1: the hardware packer's read-modify-write is NOT idempotent (or the kernel is wrong: the watcher job and the negative controls separate the two). Read
# noop_equal_* first: a written-back row that moved a stored block (the sign of a zero is the likely one) fails the SERVED writer's own idempotence, not the page writer.
# Duration (estimate): about 90 minutes runner time (each case reads the 38 MB or 71 MB caches back four times a step). Stop rule: a FAIL or NO-DECISION keeps the lever off; nothing else depends on it.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--writers page64 --widths 2052,4096 --seeds 0,1,2
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=ordered_writer IMAGE=@SERVED_IMAGE@ KOPGRAFT64=@K64J_GRAFT_DIR@ EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=@K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256@
